---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content'; import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; const areas=await getCollection('locations');
---
<BaseLayout title="Houston Remodeling Service Areas | OilerBilt" description="OilerBilt serves Houston, Alief, Mission Bend, Sugar Land, Katy and Missouri City with remodeling, drywall and painting."><div class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Service areas</div><p class="eyebrow">Where we work</p><h1>Houston and southwest Harris County.</h1><p>OilerBilt is a service-area contractor. We come to the project; there is no public showroom or customer-facing street address.</p></div></div><section><div class="wrap"><div class="service-grid">{areas.map(a=><a class="service-card" href={`/service-areas/${a.data.slug}/`}><h3>{a.data.title}</h3><p>{a.data.description}</p><span>See local details →</span></a>)}</div><article class="article"><h2>One metro, several permitting authorities</h2><p>A “Houston” mailing address does not always mean a property sits inside Houston city limits. Katy, Sugar Land and Missouri City each have their own municipal processes, while unincorporated Harris and Fort Bend county locations follow different requirements. The scope matters too: paint and cabinet replacement are not treated the same way as moving plumbing, electrical systems or structural walls.</p><p>We confirm the project address and requested changes before answering permit questions. That short check is more useful than a generic promise that every remodel needs a permit or none do.</p></article></div></section></BaseLayout>
